      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdint>\n#ifdef __ARM_NEON\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Flatten matrix into contiguous 1D array (from A)\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Integral image using single-pass construction (from B)\n    const int stride = n + 1;\n    std::vector<int64_t> ps(stride * stride, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[i * n + j];\n            ps[(i + 1) * stride + (j + 1)] = ps[i * stride + (j + 1)] + row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int64_t mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int B = 256; // block size for cache reuse (from A)\n\n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        const int base_i   = i * stride;\n        const int base_is  = (i + s) * stride;\n\n        // Loop blocking over columns (from A)\n        for (int jj = 0; jj <= n - s; jj += B) {\n            const int j_end = std::min(jj + B, n - s + 1);\n\n#ifdef __ARM_NEON\n            // NEON vectorized computation of two submatrix sums (from B)\n            int j = jj;\n            for (; j + 1 < j_end; j += 2) {\n                const int64x2_t v_a = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_is + (j + s)]);\n                const int64x2_t v_b = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_i  + (j + s)]);\n                const int64x2_t v_c = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_is + j]);\n                const int64x2_t v_d = vld1q_s64(&ps[base_i  + j]);\n\n                int64x2_t sum = vsubq_s64(v_a, v_b);\n                sum = vsubq_s64(sum, v_c);\n                sum = vaddq_s64(sum, v_d);\n\n                const int64_t s0 = vgetq_lane_s64(sum, 0);\n                const int64_t s1 = vgetq_lane_s64(sum, 1);\n                if (s0 > mxSum) mxSum = s0;\n                if (s1 > mxSum) mxSum = s1;\n            }\n            // Scalar remainder\n            for (; j < j_end; ++j)\n#else\n            // Scalar fallback (from B)\n            for (int j = jj; j < j_end; ++j)\n#endif\n            {\n                const int64_t sum_val = ps[base_is + (j + s)] - ps[base_i + (j + s)]\n                                      - ps[base_is + j] + ps[base_i + j];\n                if (sum_val > mxSum) mxSum = sum_val;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating contiguous matrix storage (A), efficient single-pass integral image construction (B), loop blocking for cache reuse (A), OpenMP parallel reduction over rows with static scheduling (B), and ARM NEON vectorized submatrix sum computation (B) yields a correct, high-performance solution on the target ARM64 platform. The algorithm change to summed-area table (C) is retained through the integral image approach.",
  "notes": "Combines all three source ideas: flattening and blocking from A; one-pass prefix construction, NEON intrinsics, and OpenMP row-wise reduction from B; parallelization and reduction pattern from C. Block size set to 256 as in A's original transformation.",
